##-*- Mode: Change-Log; coding: utf-8; -*-

v2.0.21-1 Fri, 21 Mar 2014 12:52:05 +0100 moocow
	+ replaced basename() calls with new FileBasename() wrapper to prevent cygwin build failures
	+ added AM_ICONV call for iconv support under cygwin, fixes mantis bug #656

v2.0.21 Fri, 21 Mar 2014 12:52:05 +0100 moocow
	+ fixed mantis bug #651 : bogus highlighting for near/2
	  - problem was overlapping matches some of which crossed sentence boundaries
	  - the bogus cross-boundary matches were getting mis-interpreted in CQueryNode::ConvertOccurrencesToHitsForPatterns()
	  - workaround tracks current break start as well as end, but may potentially miss some overlapping occurrences if
	    (as in the case of near()) m_Occurrences[] aren't sorted in strictly break-increasing order
	    and (as is hopefully NOT the case for near()) if the valid matches in m_Occurrences[] also arent't sorted in
	    strictly break-increasing order
	+ fixed mantis bug #652 :  context-sort not working for boolean queries (&&, ||)
	  - fix was to ensure occurrences are sorted in QueryNode.cpp CQueryBinaryOperationNode::hits_and_positions_union(), hits_and_positions_intersection()
	  - not quite kosher in #separate mode; e.g. for input "a b1 b2 c" querying (a && b* #separate) finds only "__a__ _b1_ b2 c" and
	    not "__a__ b1 _b2_ c"

v2.0.20 Wed, 19 Mar 2014 12:34:39 +0100 moocow
	+ re-worked near() queries (class CQueryNearNode in QueryNode.(cpp|h))
	  - near(a,b,c, n) now allows all match-orders abc, acb, bac, bca, cab, cba
	  - previously, near(a,b,c, n) only allowed "b"-central orders abc, cba
	+ renamed #(asc|dsc)_by_middle to #(asc|dsc)_by_middle to reflect anchor-positioning code

v2.0.20-pre4 Tue, 18 Mar 2014 12:32:54 +0100 moocow
	+ added *.opt options LemmaQueryUsesMorphPattern, DefaultQueryIndex
	+ added parsing of boolean values for *.opt options to CConcIndexator::LoadOptionsFromString()
	  - this means we can finally override pre-specified boolean flags
	+ added CConcIndexator::m_OpDefaultIndexNames : operator-specific default index names
	  - potentially useful to discriminate between "_" (bareword TokInfl queries) vs. "@_" (literal match) and "/_/" (regex, globs)
	  - idea: map "_" to "Lemma", set default expander "Lemma" to some (CAB-based) external best-lemmatizer,
	    and avoid the traffic, computational load, and loss of both precision and recall associated with
	    the current "all-inflected-forms" strategy of CQTokInfl
	+ cleaned up some lingering bigrams-index crud

v2.0.20-pre3 Mon, 17 Mar 2014 15:45:55 +0100 moocow
	+ fixed mantis bug #650: subcorpus crash caused by perl-style \x{...} escapes in escapeJsonString()
	+ fix sort-key selection for #left/#right on multi-token hits
	  - WAS: sort-key was always relative to 1st token in a multi-token hit (e.g. phrase)
	  - NOW: sort-key anchor depends on context-offset distance
	    ~ anchor is FIRST matching token of hit for #left
	    ~ anchor is FINAL matching token of hit for #right
	    ~ anchor is MIDDLE matching token of hit for #context (i0 + (iN-i0)/2)

v2.0.20-pre2 Mon, 17 Mar 2014 13:08:43 +0100 moocow
	+ updated querydoc for new operators
	+ added implicit conjunction of concatenated qc_basic query clauses (no boolean ops)
	  - (@foo @bar) works, (@foo @bar && !@baz) works, but (@foo @bar !@baz) is a parse error
	  - problem is (q_clause . q_filters) and "negated" filters like !#HAS_FIELD
	+ fixed reduce/reduce conflict in qfb_ctxsort / qfb_ctxjey : token attribtes should match sym_str
	  - i.e. SYMBOL and not INTEGER or DATE

v2.0.20-pre1 Fri, 14 Mar 2014 10:36:51 +0100 moocow
	+ added query flags #(no)join/#(no)separate : do/don't return at most 1 hit per container (sentence; default=do (compat))
	+ code was already basically in place in QueryNode.cpp, just needed to be raised to user level

v2.0.19-2 Wed, 12 Mar 2014 09:05:45 +0100 moocow
	+ bugfix: apply filter bounds for m_SortOrder==0 in CConcHolder::GetAllHits()
	+ fixes bogus results for (@am #has[corpus,/core/]) in dta

v2.0.19-1 Fri, 07 Mar 2014 15:54:10 +0100 moocow
	+ bugfix: use stable_sort() for merged hit-list sorting in CDDCServerListenHost::RunDistributed()
	+ ensures that HitNo order is preserved (otherwise segfaults ensue)

v2.0.19 Fri, 07 Mar 2014 13:04:47 +0100 moocow
	+ overhauled hit-sorting and filtering both subcorpus-locally and in distrib<->subcorpus communications
	  - sort-key field moved from integer to new compound struct CHitSortKey {int i; string s;}
	    * primary sort by integer, secondary by string
	  - subcorpus-local hit-sorting (esp in ConcHolder.cpp) uses integer sort keys (fast, mostly old code)
	  - distributed server now sorts only by string key (although string key may be an encoded integer)
	  - CConcHolder now has m_SortOrder, m_bSortByString fields
	    * added fields to CQueryResult (cached query results)
	    * otherwise get weird 0-hits on final query of "... #asc_date" "... #dsc_date" "... #asc_date"
	      : b/c data is coming from cache with correct order-info, but not getting sorted properly by the CConcHolder
		due to stale CConcHolder flags m_SortOrder, m_bSortByString
	  - potential problems/improvements
	    * distributed server could do a merge-sort on hits from subcorpora, but it just waits and does a quick-sort
	    * sort-key strings are allocated and copied for each filter application in ConcHolder::GetAllHits(),
	      but we might be able to just wait and copy strings of the *last* filter
	    * sort-key strings are sent over the network to the server; this can cause a lot of traffic especially for
	      large sort keys (e.g. title) in combination with large result sets
		+ removed old 'Bigrams' index and extrusions
	+ got replacement #left/#right sort operators working as aliases for new offset-based #(asc|desc)_by_context
	  - added key-attribute field argument to #left/#right (analagous to #less_by[*])
	  - added key-offset argument to #left/#right (analagous to #less_by[*])
	  - added lower-/upper-bound arguments to #left/#right (analagous to #less_by[BIBL,*,*])
	  - updated query docs
	+ un-method-fied string_socket.h functions (since they're also used by ddc_search pseudo-cgi)

v2.0.18 Wed, 19 Feb 2014 12:27:34 +0100 moocow
	+ added ddc_proto(5) manpage
	+ implemented new server commands "version", "status", "vstatus", "info"
	+ src/ConcordDmnLib/Corpora.cpp minor beautifications
	+ updated copyright notices in source files
	+ updated date-string parsing code in CBibliography::ConvertDateToInt():
	  - allow YYYY-MM(-DD)? with MM > 12
	  - allow YYYY-MM with no DD
	  - allow YYYY-MM-DD with DD > 31
	  - allow YYYY up to 65535 (limit for encoding)

v2.0.17 Tue, 11 Feb 2014 12:58:18 +0100 moocow
	+ agramtab, morphwizardlib, ddc_morph_gen: fixes for morphology compilation
	  - symptom: Morph/*/npredict.bin has size 1130 for all languages
	  - symptom: German 'Vaterland', 'Plastikflasche' are not expanded, but 'Land' and 'Flasche' are
	  - problem: ddc_morph_gen wants e.g. RML/dict/Morph/ggramtab.tab but that doesn't exist yet at compile time
	    (path RML/dict/morph/ggramtab.tab is pseudo-hard-coded in RML/etc/rml.ini)
	  - workaround: added a key 'GRAMTAB' to *.mwz files read by ddc_morph_gen: if that file exists, it's preferred to the registry file
	+ complete fix also requires new ddc-morph v2.0.1

